<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!--
    Camps' cross-section surface, carved into its own leaf project rather than a Contracts/
    folder for two independent reasons. Base consumes it: ShiftManagementService reads
    CampSeasonInfo, SystemTeamSyncJob takes the two camp-lead reads, and Shell's
    ProfileSummaryViewModelBuilder binds CampUserInfo. And Camps and CityPlanning reference
    each other — CampService clears a deleted camp's polygons through
    Lazy<ICityPlanningService> while CityPlanningService injects ICampServiceRead — so a
    folder would be a project cycle (design §15.5b,
    memory/architecture/section-project-cycle-fix.md).

    It holds exactly what lives outside the section: the read surface eight moved sections and
    Base inject, the two camp-lead reads SystemTeamSyncJob used to take off ICampRepository,
    the verbs Humans.Development's two dev seeders drive, and the flat projections those
    signatures name. The directory, detail, admin, roster, join-request, role-management,
    compliance, image and early-entry DTOs are internal to the section.

    The five camp enums live here rather than in the section's internal Domain/ because the
    leaf's own records name them (Budget's rule). Teams' hard floor does not apply: no
    Humans.UI partial renders any of them — _CampCard.cshtml is the section's own view.

    References Humans.Interfaces (IApplicationService) and Humans.Domain (the shared camp
    facility enums — SoundZone, SpaceSize, ElectricalGrid, YesNoMaybe and friends — which stay
    Base vocabulary because Shell and other sections spell them). Acyclic: Humans.Domain names
    only Humans.Interfaces.
  -->

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\Humans.Interfaces\Humans.Interfaces.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\Humans.Domain\Humans.Domain.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="NodaTime" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
